cies of  insects  our team is doing some  lab and field research to find different  potential edible insects across  madagascar  dr fisher created the project in 2006  after years studying madagascar's  declining forests  the scale of the threat from the  country's hungry human population dawned  on him i wanted to explore the forest  and find all the undiscovered insects in  madagascar but along the way i realized  that  these people have no choice if they want  to feed their kids they're going to have  to cut the forest and grow a crop on it  for one or two years today  only 10 to 15 percent of madagascar's  original forests survive and its  endangered species continue to be hunted  for food  global warming is also severely  affecting the food supply here  [Music]  in 2021  madagascar suffered from what's been  called the world's first climate change  famine thousands of people are in brink  of starvation  so that's why we started this project  in response valala farms is scaling up  production and planning to open a new  facility in 2022  [Music]  it aims to mass produce cricket powder  with 54 protein per 100 grams  that's twice the level of protein found  in chicken  the product is already being trialled in  places such as this orphanage where the  insect powder is added to porridge  and where the benefits of qriket farming  are taught in classes  one study in madagascar found a 50  reduction in bush meat hunting following  the introduction of cricket farming our  model madagascar can expand to feed a  millions of people in madagascar but  also could expand to feed 5 million  people in africa  the same  system will work in almost anywhere  there's food insecurity biodiversity  issues and climate change  it's a solution that actually works in a  small village  and one day it's going to reach the  store next to you  but there is a fly in the ointment  for insects to hit supermarket shells in  the west and beyond  farming will have to be industrialized  and scaled